# Haunted House
#
# This source recreates the classic Haunted House adventure from
# "Write Your Own Adventure Programs" in MuseLang. The room layout,
# objects, treasures and puzzle structure closely follow the original
# BASIC program.
#
# A PDF of the book is available:
# https://usborne.com/au/books/computer-and-coding-books
#
# The original game relies on several features which are not currently
# available in MuseLang V1, including:
#
#   * conditional exits (doors, barriers and hazards which dynamically
#     enable or disable movement)
#   * random events and probabilistic encounters
#   * arithmetic variables and score calculations
#   * turn counters and timers
#   * global verb definitions independent of objects
#
# Where these mechanics are required, they have been expressed using the
# facilities currently available in MuseLang, primarily object state,
# object interactions and descriptive text. This keeps the adventure
# playable while remaining a useful reference for future MuseLang
# language development.

